      "title": "serveStatic can read files outside its root on Windows when a path holds encoded backslashes",
      "found_by": null,
      "reported_by": null,
      "module_name": "hono",
      "cves": [],
      "vulnerable_versions": "<4.11.2",
      "patched_versions": ">=4.11.2",
      "overview": "On Windows, the serveStatic middleware decoded a percent-encoded backslash after checking the path against its root, so a request such as /css/..%5c..%5cconfig could read files outside the static folder. Servers on Linux and macOS are not affected, since the backslash is not a path separator there.",
